A weight module over $Y^{\lambda}_{\mu}$ (resp. $FY^{\lambda}_{\mu}$ ) is a module $M$ for which the subalgebra $P^{\Sigma}$ (resp. $P$ ) acts locally finitely with finite-dimensional generalized eigenspaces.

Let $M$ be a weight module for $Y^{\lambda}_{\mu}$. So we can write

$\displaystyle M= igoplus_{\mathbf{S}\in\operatorname{Spec}P^{\Sigma}}W_{\mathbf{S}}(M)$

$\displaystyle W_{\mathbf{S}}(M)= ig\{v\in M:\exists N	ext{ s.t. }(f-ev_{\mathbf{S}}(f))^{N}v=0	ext{ for all }f\in P^{\Sigma} ig\}$

We refer to $W_{\mathbf{S}}(M)$ as the $\mathbf{S}$ -weight space of $M$ and we say that $M\mapsto W_{\mathbf{S}}(M)$ is a weight functor. Similarly, for a module $M$ over $FY^{\lambda}_{\mu}$, we define $W_{ m{
