Considering the adjoint action of the dots on the flag Yangian, we see that if a module $M$ is generated by finitely many weight vectors, then every other weight that appears will lie in the affine Weyl group orbit of the original weights. Since integral weights are closed under the action of the affine Weyl group, we could equivalently define ${FY^{\lambda}_{\mu}\operatorname{-wtmod}}$ to be the category of weight modules generated by vectors of integral weight.

